Version 2.0
===========
* Changed output of influence list, each level (delete or outlier) previously has a sublist called class.out/class.del and param.out/param.del.  This has now been changed to segment and param.
* Added the option of k points to be modified into loo and moo (and parent functions to pass down)
* Added arguments to main functions to allow the user to pick which subset of points are starting points (in conjunction with k sequential) to modify.  This includes "all" which gives the previous behaviour, "random" (uniform), "stratified" (by segment), or a vector of indices.
* Streamlined the backend functions (loo, moo)
* Expanded use of the influence function to allows users to specify any changepoint method (with expectations on input and output formats)


* Moved the influence method to a function with S4 object output influenceCpt
* Changed the plotting functions to be methods for influenceCpt
* Made new plot, summary and print functions for influenceCpt class
* Added option of "difference" to inflence map so it can be plotted without the expected.
* Allowed the use of changepoint methods that don't return parameter estimates

Version 1.0.1
=============
* Changed itemize to describe in InfluenceMap.Rd - CRAN check
* Removed generic use of influence(model,...) from usage area in influence-methods.Rd - CRAN check
* Updated format of NEWS to comply with new CRAN checks
* Updated references throughout to JCGS citation instead of ArXiV

